# Cursor Rules — Hashtagweb3.com Coding Agent Rules

You are an AI coding agent assisting with the Hashtagweb3.com codebase.

## Codebase Principles
- Framework: Next.js 14 App Router (TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS & Lucide Icons
- Database & Storage: Supabase (PostgreSQL), static jobs cache (`content/jobs-cache.json`)
- Deployment: Vercel

## API Conventions
- Public REST APIs located under `src/app/api/` (CORS enabled `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`).
- OpenAPI spec: `public/openapi.json`.
- All JSON errors follow standard envelope: `{ "error": { "code": string, "message": string, "docUrl": string } }`.

## Agent Capabilities & Endpoints
- LLMs Index: `/llms.txt`
- MCP Product Server: `/api/mcp` and `/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json`
- MCP Docs Server: `/api/mcp-docs` and `/.well-known/mcp-docs/server-card.json`
- Agent Plugin Manifest: `/.well-known/plugin.json`
- WorkOS Agent Auth: `/auth.md`

## Coding Standards
- Do NOT introduce breaking API schema changes without updating `openapi.json` and `llms.txt`.
- Server Components by default; add `'use client'` only for interactive components.
